win32u: force recalculating the menu bar height in get_menu_bar_height

Upstream Wine b94b54c62b (2026-11-03, after 11.21), backported unchanged.
Wine 11.20's f3de8edf99 made get_menu_bar_height() go through
NtUserDrawMenuBarTemp(), which lays the menu bar out only when its cached
height is 0. WM_NCCALCSIZE therefore kept the layout of the first width the
menu bar was measured at: a window whose menu was set while it was small
kept its menu wrapped into many rows after it grew (Notepad++: the menu bar
in 8 rows of 2 items in a 1100 px wide window).

--- a/dlls/win32u/menu.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/menu.c
@@ -2240,11 +2240,14 @@
 UINT get_menu_bar_height( HWND hwnd, UINT width, INT org_x, INT org_y )
 {
     RECT rect = { org_x, org_y, org_x + width, 0 };
+    struct menu *menu;
     UINT height;
     HDC hdc;
 
     TRACE( "hwnd %p, width %d, at (%d, %d).\n", hwnd, width, org_x, org_y );
 
+    if ((menu = unsafe_menu_ptr( get_menu( hwnd )))) menu->Height = 0; /* force size recalculate */
+
     hdc = NtUserGetDCEx( hwnd, 0, DCX_CACHE | DCX_WINDOW );
     height = NtUserDrawMenuBarTemp( hwnd, hdc, &rect, 0, 0 );
     NtUserReleaseDC( hwnd, hdc );
